y value above 100 but lower than your current chips.].\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Evaluation:\nLet me analyze the current situation:\n\n**My Hand:** 8♥ Q♠\n**Board:** 7♣ Q♥ 6♥ 3♥\n**Current Hand:** Pair of Queens (top pair, decent kicker with 8)\n\n**Pot Analysis:**\n- Pre-flop: Both checked (big blind/small blind only)\n- Flop: I raised 500, opponent called\n- Turn: Opponent checked to me\n\n**Draw Possibilities:**\n1. I have a flush draw (3 hearts on board, 1 in hand = 4/9 outs for flush)\n2. Possible straight draws on board (7-6-3 with gaps)\n3. My pair of Queens is currently top pair\n\n**Opponent's Likely Holdings:**\n- Checking throughout suggests: weak pair, drawing hand, or slow-playing\n- If they had a strong hand (set, two pair, or made flush), they likely would have bet the turn\n- Could have: smaller pair, weak Queen, flush draw, or straight draw\n\n**Strategic Considerations:**\n- I'm ahead in cumulative chips (+1800)\n- This is hand 13/20, still mid-game\n- I have top pair with reasonable kicker\n- The turn brought another heart (4 hearts on board is dangerous)\n- Opponent's passive play suggests weakness\n\n**Promising Moves:**\n1. **Check (0):** Pot control, see river cheaply, but allows free card\n2. **Bet ~300-500:** Value bet, protects hand, gets info\n3. **Bet ~800-1000:** Larger bet for protection and value\n4. **All-in (-2):** Too aggressive for top pair with this board texture\n\nReason:\nI should make a value bet of around 600-800 chips. My pair of Queens is likely ahead given opponent's passive play, but the board is dangerous with 4 hearts showing. A medium-sized bet accomplishes multiple goals: extracts value from worse hands (smaller pairs, weak Queens), protects against draws, and doesn't overcommit if opponent has a flush or better. Checking is too passive and gives a free river card. All-in is excessive for top pair on this coordinated board.\n\nAnswer: 700"}
