** Too aggressive; only gets called by better hands\n\nReason:\nMy Queen-high flush is strong, and opponent's passive play throughout all streets suggests they likely have a medium-strength hand (pair, two pair, or possibly a lower flush). Checking gives up value. A moderate bet of around 1200-1500 chips extracts value from hands that will call (like a pair of Queens with worse kicker, a straight, or lower flush) while not overcommitting if they surprisingly have a better flush. Given the pot has grown through my betting and their calls, a bet of approximately 1200 seems optimal.\n\nAnswer: 1200"}
